From 1f6e5981a54d17da07a62385262290c0deb123e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hanbang <hanbang@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:33:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] NGP Dual: link cable for two consoles in one core

- mednafen/ngp/hb_link.c: when hb_link_on, emulate serial channel 0
  (SC0BUF/SC0CR/SC0MOD/BR0CR, 0xB2 RTS, CTS handshake, INTRX0=0x6FE4,
  INTTX0=0x6FE8) and implement the BIOS COM calls on the BIOS work RAM
  rings used by the games own SIO handlers (0x6C80/0x6CC0/0x6D00..06).
  RTC reads a base time + emulated cycles (in the state) instead of the
  host clock. Off by default: identical to upstream NeoPop.
- libretro.c: line-stepping API (hb_ngp_*) and save name/fallback/write
  control for the second console.
- dual/: Beetle NeoPop Dual wrapper (two inner copies renamed with
  objcopy, line-interleaved, fixed-size state, 1P/2P screen option).

